{"ts":"2026-08-14T05:43:43.033Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"5eb0c73a26456fbf7755e52f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-14T05:43:43.033Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-14T05:43:43.033Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Implemented: fetchAllItems now throws CommandError on any pm list-all failure (non-zero status, spawn error, ENOBUFS overrun, unparseable JSON) instead of degrading to []. Added pmJsonMaxBuffer (64 MiB, PM_JSON_MAX_BUFFER override) and describePmReadFailure matching the pm-jira/pm-todos convention, resolvePmBin to use the project-local @unbrained/pm-cli pm shim with PATH fallback, and an explicit maxBuffer. 16 new tests cover each failure shape, binary resolution, and a command-path regression test (runExporter) proving pm standup export exits non-zero on a failed read. Revert experiment confirmed the regression test fails (Missing expected rejection) with the old return [] restored."}]}],"before_hash":"55ba768acc5f0b52501419cb6a6534f58fd9a0306e126deb23c36b1205a203ea","after_hash":"c64c3885ef2bddb96ac9a932ed4ba6c51bb36e5fcaee6b625bbc5c099a2491c2","item_hash_version":2}
